List shows:

  ls -l /home/light/shows/

From the Mac:

  ./scripts/upload-show.sh --list


------------------------------------------------------------
UPLOAD SHOW FROM MAC
------------------------------------------------------------

Run on the Mac, not inside Shield SSH:

  cd /Users/miiroseppanen/shieldxl-light-console

  ./scripts/upload-show.sh "/path/to/show.qxw"

  ./scripts/upload-show.sh --dry-run "/path/to/show.qxw"
  ./scripts/upload-show.sh --replace "/path/to/show.qxw"
  ./scripts/upload-show.sh --list

The helper validates the .qxw, writes a Shield-safe patched copy
(Art-Net forced to 127.0.0.1 Line 0), and copies that copy only.
The original/source file on the Mac is not modified.
An invalid project is rejected and does not replace a working
project. Without --replace, current.qxw is left unchanged.


------------------------------------------------------------
MANUAL FILE COPY
------------------------------------------------------------

These scp commands are run from the Mac terminal.

FROM MAC TO SHIELD:

  scp "/path/to/file.qxw" \
    light@shieldxl-light.local:/home/light/

For show projects, prefer ./scripts/upload-show.sh instead of
copying directly into /home/light/shows/ or onto current.qxw.

FROM SHIELD TO MAC:

  scp light@shieldxl-light.local:/home/light/<file> .


------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT / REPOSITORY
------------------------------------------------------------

Runtime/deploy path:
  /home/light/light-console

